# The Python here is the *test oracle*, not the product.
#
# `xtask/golden/` runs diffusers/transformers to dump reference tensors, and
# measures the reference's own f32 noise floor so a tolerance can be derived
# rather than guessed. Nothing ships with it and `cargo build` never invokes
# it — but it is the reason this project can say "verified against diffusers"
# instead of "looks right".
#
# Excluded from the language statistics because it is tooling. Deleting 38k
# lines of Rust when candle went tripled Python's apparent share of a
# repository whose Python did not change at all, which is exactly the kind of
# number that misleads at a glance.
xtask/golden/*.py linguist-detectable=false

# Generated fixtures and reference images are data, not source.
tests/golden/** linguist-generated=true
assets/*.png binary
